        "id": "c0ffee00rrtab2",
        "type": "tab",
        "label": "Roborock dedicated nodes",
        "disabled": false,
        "info": "Dedicated Roborock nodes sharing one device. Set up the device (account, fetch, IP) before deploying."
    },
    {
        "id": "c0ffee00rrcomment02",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "c0ffee00rrtab2",
        "name": "How to use this example",
        "info": "1. Open the roborock device config, add a roborock account, sign in, fetch the vacuum, set the IP, and click Done. Deploy once.\n2. command: start / dock. status: output 1 is the status, output 2 is events (cleaning-started, cleaning-finished, error, error-cleared, low-battery).\n3. clean rooms: after the device is deployed, open the node and use Pick rooms from the robot. The floor is stored with the rooms.\n4. consumables: checked once a day; the second output only fires for worn parts.\n\nThe universal roborock-vacuum node is still there for new or undocumented commands.\nlocal_key is stored in credentials and is not part of this example.\nThis package is unofficial and is not affiliated with Roborock.",
        "x": 260,
        "y": 60,
        "wires": []
    },
